1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,392
My family sends money home to Haiti every month.

2
00:00:03,442 --> 00:00:07,515
Texts like this one arrive every week: your transfer is on hold,

3
00:00:07,565 --> 00:00:10,221
send the six-digit code in thirty minutes.

4
00:00:10,271 --> 00:00:13,893
The people who get them are our parents and grandparents.

5
00:00:13,943 --> 00:00:16,019
They need a second opinion, fast.

6
00:00:16,069 --> 00:00:19,240
But these are the most private messages they have.

7
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:24,516
Veye, which means watch out in Haitian Kreyòl, is a scam checker

8
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:26,724
that asks your own device first.

9
00:00:26,774 --> 00:00:31,072
It is built on Firebase AI Logic hybrid inference: local rules,

10
00:00:31,122 --> 00:00:35,212
then Gemini Nano on the device, and Gemini in the cloud only

11
00:00:35,262 --> 00:00:38,800
when it is needed, with personal data removed first.

12
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:44,635
Sign in, and Veye shows the on-device model status, today's

13
00:00:44,685 --> 00:00:48,769
checks, scams caught, and how many personal items were kept

14
00:00:48,819 --> 00:00:49,330
private.

15
00:00:52,050 --> 00:00:54,075
Here is that remittance text.

16
00:00:54,125 --> 00:00:58,582
Smart mode, English. Gemini Nano reads it right here in Chrome,

17
00:00:58,632 --> 00:01:01,015
on a laptop with no graphics card.

18
00:01:01,065 --> 00:01:04,664
Scam, ninety percent: a fake money transfer notice.

19
00:01:04,714 --> 00:01:09,028
The red flags in plain words, what to do next, and the badge:

20
00:01:09,078 --> 00:01:11,317
on this device, zero bytes sent.

21
00:01:11,367 --> 00:01:14,680
And Veye shows exactly why it ran where it did.

22
00:01:15,583 --> 00:01:19,488
Now a lottery scam in Kreyòl, with the answer in Kreyòl.

23
00:01:19,538 --> 00:01:23,654
Gemini Nano does not answer in Kreyòl yet, so Veye's router

24
00:01:23,704 --> 00:01:28,031
switches to the cloud through the same Firebase AI Logic call.

25
00:01:28,081 --> 00:01:32,268
But first, on the device, it removes personal data, here the

26
00:01:32,318 --> 00:01:36,363
sender's phone number. The badge says it: cloud, redacted.

27
00:01:37,283 --> 00:01:39,622
Many scams arrive as screenshots.

28
00:01:39,672 --> 00:01:44,110
This fake delivery text is read on the device too, with Gemini

29
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:48,598
Nano's image input: a suspicious link, a tiny fee, a deadline.

30
00:01:48,648 --> 00:01:52,869
A screenshot cannot be redacted, so Veye never sends one to

31
00:01:52,919 --> 00:01:55,113
the cloud without asking first.

32
00:01:58,217 --> 00:02:01,965
The same engine runs in a Chrome extension: a side panel that

33
00:02:02,015 --> 00:02:05,949
checks the page you are on, and a warning badge from local rules

34
00:02:05,999 --> 00:02:08,627
on every site, with no network call at all.

35
00:02:11,717 --> 00:02:15,917
App Check with a custom provider protects the AI, even inside

36
00:02:15,967 --> 00:02:20,237
the extension. Remote Config changes routing and scam patterns

37
00:02:20,287 --> 00:02:24,835
without a new build. And Veye stores no message and no screenshot,

38
00:02:24,885 --> 00:02:28,807
ever. Veye. Before you answer, ask your own device first.
